Stage 5 S5-07 — bounded UART stack-context diagnostic, live N=2 evidence
Date: 2026-11-15

Purpose
=======
Exercise the opt-in `--stack-context-out` diagnostic on the saved stage4a
`--set-cpl0 --user-mode` profile and determine whether its samples correlate
with the Linux panic trace. These are two separate single-run invocations;
the diagnostic is forbidden in series mode, and these runs were not passed to
the series comparator. They do not constitute S5-07 acceptance.

Inputs and invocation profile
=============================
Kernel SHA-256:    9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e
Initramfs SHA-256: ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588
ACPI blob SHA-256: b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf
ACPI manifest SHA-256: 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2

Both runs used `stage4a --set-cpl0 --user-mode`, 128 MiB RAM, counted mode,
retirement budget 3,000,000,000, expected stop `budget_exhausted`, and
`diagnostic_past_c7=false`. The release runner was built from clean commit
`79fa6ad1c00295d89a31d11bc772894af8a78596` on macOS/aarch64. The standalone
runner JSON does not include source revision. Each run used a different nonce.

Results
=======

| Run | Nonce suffix | Retired | Stop | #PF | #GP(0) | IRQ0 edges / total IRQ deliveries | UART bytes | Samples | Write error |
|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 0001 | 001 | 2,999,999,998 | budget_exhausted | 34 | 1 | 34,810 / 34,815 | 23,775 | 4 | null |
| 0002 | 002 | 2,999,999,998 | budget_exhausted | 33 | 1 | 34,815 / 34,820 | 23,803 | 4 | null |

Each run reached the guest, emitted its exact nonce marker once, and produced
four snapshots. Every snapshot contained 10 reliable symbol+offset trace
frames whose addresses exactly matched captured frame-pointer return
addresses. No optional `?` frame matched. Each sidecar's first-trigger chain
contained the same 23 addresses; each chain ended at `null_frame_pointer`.
The sidecar is explicitly `capture_scope=console-output context` and
`unwind_context=false`; this is correlation evidence, not a full unwinder.

The debug ELF used for symbol correlation was
`/Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/vms/s2-00-ubuntu-26.04.1/vmlinux-debug-7.0.0-38-generic`,
SHA-256 `7e460f048c3de0f8ee85fd326f2f65d95a6ee448e57b6f5333e2be79b5be9d1f`,
BuildID `338e542e384c46228f7a378babc0f9bb2b6a5997`. Its `.text` and the exact
decompressed kernel payload `.text` were both 24,408,304 bytes with SHA-256
`5dec4d30f388386c69c39474841b80ceef957d7a0a3aa2eb2561cb64703e9961`.
All 10 reliable frames resolved against that ELF. The optional candidates
were not in the sampled active chain in these snapshots; this does not prove
that all optional frames are invalid or safe to ignore.

